 "id": "2026-huang-longxing",
 "name": "Longxing heritage buildings: cultural value scale (CVES)",
 "description": "Replication of Huang, H., Mat Sulaiman, M. K. A., Harun, N. Z., He, W., & Wen, B. (2026). An evaluation scale for the cultural value of heritage buildings. PLOS ONE 21(6): e0350924. Respondents look at photos of five heritage buildings in Longxing Ancient Town, Chongqing (Liu Family Ancestral Hall, Liu Family Courtyard, Huaxia Ancestral Hall, Longxing Temple, Longzang Palace), one at a time, and score each on the paper's 24-item Cultural Value Evaluation Scale (Table 5: local, scientific, historic, aesthetic and sustainability value), 1–5 with the paper's anchors (very unconcerned … very concerned). Demographics follow Table 9 (gender, age band, academic qualifications, occupational category). Analysis as in the paper: item and dimension means, Cronbach's alpha, KMO/Bartlett and PCA with varimax (five factors); the paper's AHP weights (Table 8) can be applied. Photos: the paper's Figure 3 (authors' own photos, CC BY 4.0), cropped only to remove the panel letters; credited on every page, and the template is removed if the authors object.\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) one photo per building (the paper's Figure 3) instead of the three photo groups per building (overall, close range, interior) used in the survey, which were not published; (2) online survey instead of visitors approached in the town with a QR code; (3) buildings appear in random order (order not reported); (4) the consent line, introduction and instructions are our wording; (5) statement U31 (\"The tour gave me…\") is kept as written although online respondents did not tour the town.",
 "author": "Huang, Mat Sulaiman, Harun, He & Wen",
